div.p:
It was agreed: 

—to issue a NSSM calling for a study of the general question of naval
                            arms control;


—that we are not prepared to accept any deployment limitations on
                            SSBNs in the Indian Ocean;

—to prepare a more specific paper on the question of naval deployment
                            limitations for presenation to the President, and that nothing would be
                            discussed with any government prior to a Presidential decision;

—State will prepare talking points for the President’s meeting with
                            Prime Minister Bandaranaike and obtain agency views on them;


—our instructions to our UN Delegation on the Ceylonese proposal will
                            be based on the President’s conversation with Mrs. Bandaranaike.
